## Quick start (no API keys, no infrastructure)

```bash
python -m venv .venv
. .venv/bin/activate                                  # Windows: .venv\Scripts\activate
pip install --require-hashes -r requirements-dev.lock
pip install -e . --no-deps
cp .env.example .env                                  # Windows: copy .env.example .env
```

Edit `.env`: set `MODEL_PROVIDER=offline`{% if uses_postgres %}, `DATABASE_URL=sqlite:///./var/agent.db`,
`CHECKPOINT_BACKEND=sqlite`{% if retrieval.store == "pgvector" %} and `VECTOR_STORE=memory`{% endif %}{% endif %}, then start the API:

```bash
uvicorn src.api.main:app --reload --port 8000           # interactive docs: http://localhost:8000/docs
```

`MODEL_PROVIDER=offline` is a deterministic heuristic model, so the whole workflow — tools,
retrieval, approvals, guardrails — runs without credentials. Switch to `{{ model.provider }}`
(`{{ model.model }}`) for real use{% if model.provider == "local" %}: start Ollama with
`docker compose --profile local-llm up -d ollama`, then `docker compose exec ollama ollama pull {{ model.model }}`{% endif %}.
`make install`, `make run`, `make test` and `make evals` wrap the same commands.

