## Using the API

```bash
# 1. Start a run (caller key)
curl -s localhost:8000/v1/runs -H "X-API-Key: change-me-dev-key" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"message": {{ sample_request|json }}}'

# 2. If status is "awaiting_approval", review pending_approval.actions, then decide (approver key)
curl -s localhost:8000/v1/runs/<run_id>/approval -H "X-API-Key: change-me-approver-key" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"approved": true, "reviewer": "Your Name"}'
```

| Endpoint | Purpose |
| --- | --- |
| `POST /v1/runs` | Start a run (`message`, optional `thread_id` for conversation memory) |
| `GET /v1/runs/{run_id}` | Run state; `?include_audit=true` adds the audit trail |
| `POST /v1/runs/{run_id}/approval` | Approve or reject pending actions (approver key; optional `action_ids` for partial approval) |
| `DELETE /v1/threads/{thread_id}/memory` | Erase a conversation (approver key) |
| `GET /health`, `GET /ready`, `GET /metrics` | Operations |

The CLI offers the same flow: `python -m src.cli run "<request>" --approve --reviewer "Dana"`.

