## Tools

| Tool | Mode | Approval | Inputs | Description |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
{%- for tool in tools %}
| `{{ tool.name }}` | {{ tool.mode }} | {{ "required" if tool.approval_required else "—" }} | {{ tool.input_summary|md }} | {{ tool.description|md }} |
{%- endfor %}

*read* tools run during the workflow; *draft* tools prepare side-effect-free previews and commit
only after approval; *execute* tools never run before approval. Approvals bind to a SHA-256
digest of the exact tool arguments, which is re-verified immediately before execution.

### Connecting real systems

Development uses `TOOL_BACKEND=fixture` (sample data in `data/fixtures/tools.json`). For
production set `TOOL_BACKEND=http` and implement this contract in a small gateway in front of your
systems of record:

```
POST {TOOL_BACKEND_URL}/tools/{tool}/{phase}        phase ∈ read | preview | execute
Authorization: Bearer {TOOL_BACKEND_TOKEN}
Idempotency-Key: {run_id}:{tool}:{digest}             (execute only)
{"arguments": {...}, "run_id": "...", "request_id": "..."}  ->  JSON object
```

Or replace the `handle` function in `src/tools/<tool>.py` to call an SDK directly; input models
in the same file keep validation in place.
