`tests/integration` covers the HTTP API, graph topology and the MCP server; `tests/agent` runs
end-to-end workflow, approval and adversarial scenarios.

## Security model

- Requests, retrieved documents and tool outputs are untrusted data; they are scanned for
  prompt injection and framed as data in prompts.
- Tools are allowlisted (`src/tools/catalog.py`), schema-validated, phase-checked and time-limited
  ({{ guardrails.tool_timeout_seconds }}s default, {{ guardrails.max_tool_calls }} calls per run).
- Side effects require a human decision from an **approver key**; callers cannot approve.
- Approvals are bound to argument digests, so a modified action is never executed.
- Production refuses to start with default keys, the offline model, fixture tools or in-memory
  checkpoints (`ENV=production`).

